AUDIO: 'You can use command code to write tests for you. Just point it at a file or a feature. First, it studies the code to understand what it does, works out which tests are needed, and writes them. From there, it runs them. And if anything'

[00:13] [scene:test_run]
VISUAL: Test results show "1 failed, 2 passed", with "rejects an expired session" failing Test results show "1 failed, 2 passed", with "rejects an expired session" failing, expected `401`, received `SessionExpiredError` Command Code identifies the error: "Expired sessions throw SessionExpiredError, not a 401 - fixing the assertion." Command Code applies a fix, changing `toThrow('401')` to `toThrow(SessionExpiredError)` in `auth.test.ts` Tests are re-run after the fix All 3 tests pass after the fix Terminal shows all tests passed, and the prompt returns "Command Code" title card with the terminal showing the previous command On-screen text shows `npm i -g command-code` for installation
AUDIO: 'fails, it reads the error, fixes it, and runs the tests again until the whole suite passes. Why not try it on your next untested file?'
